  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Two bodies move along a straight path, starting at the same time, so their displacement $x$ m from a fixed point $O$ at any time $t$ is given by $x=t+6$ and $x=t^2+4$ respectively. At what times are they:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=2\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "The bodies are together when their displacements are equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}t+6&=t^2+4\\\\t^2-t-2&=0\\\\(t-2)(t+1)&=0\\\\t&=2\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nSince time is measured from their common start, $t\\geq0$. Hence $t=2\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Travelling with the same velocity?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=0.5\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "Differentiating the displacement functions gives $v_1=1$ and $v_2=2t$. For equal velocities,\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=2t\\\\t&=\\frac12\\text{ s}\\\\t&=0.5\\text{ s}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
